event_uuid":"4b271f96-35c0-41ab-81f4-26deb19077b5","position":{"commit_sha":"816ea0bc5d45242e2310526831d31bdddfcee870","position":"1793826212887334738-4b271f96-35c0-41ab-81f4-26deb19077b5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"93101dd12bafad75e42b65104895a2463a808233e0ec89983ab5c808f934295f","event_uuid":"5dd05028-286f-4f67-b661-4f737f68c979","position":{"commit_sha":"12440c2552839575a3e05e93f0246a43d05c8961","position":"1793826703708165853-5dd05028-286f-4f67-b661-4f737f68c979"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"73820003a9383bcaca67048b7f8054bbd9abccb10cb2ba028449215f5f27174c","event_uuid":"14773d02-82e5-45e3-9508-1aa53d585707","position":{"commit_sha":"12440c2552839575a3e05e93f0246a43d05c8961","position":"1793826703792445663-14773d02-82e5-45e3-9508-1aa53d585707"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793824949117638944,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\nA read-based documentation audit (independently verified twice: once by the auditing agent,\nonce by the operator) found one consistent defect class across ~143k LOC: comments/docstrings\nthat were true when written and are now false -- costly for LLM agents, which treat a comment as\nauthoritative and burn context chasing a dangling pointer.\n\nScoped to 9 verified sites + a read-only census of a 10th excluded family (\"Parser of record\").\nBehaviour-preserving only: comment/docstring corrections, 2 same-file statement moves, 1\ndead-assignment deletion, 1 new self-checking test. No control-flow changes. Re-verify every\nsite against current origin/main before editing (audit base was 2e28d817a7e); skip+report any\nsite that no longer matches.\n\n## Sites\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py` ~12-30 + constant block: wrongly claims\n   `_STEP_VERIFY`/`_STEP_DECIDE`/`_LLM_STEP_KINDS` mirror `gate_dispatch.py` (which defines none\n   of them). Real home: `src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py` (L20/21/70). 3rd copy\n   of `_LLM_STEP_KINDS` at `runs.py:393` w/ differently-worded comment. Fix: correct both\n   comments to name `plan_review_recovery` as canonical, note the `runs.py` copy, preserve the\n   stated reason for duplication (finalize.py stays a leaf, no back-import). Add a plain test\n   (no new fixture/helper) asserting the 3-way constant equality, in the existing natural test\n   home if one exists.\n\n2. `src/rebar/reducer/_api.py`: `_NON_GRAPH_ARTIFACT_TYPES` has 3 members; comment names only 2\n   (`identity` added by b665cff905d without updating prose), plus 4 inherited stale-2-type sites:\n   a docstring in `_api.py`, `graph/_ready.py` ~92-94, `graph/_unblock.py` ~167-170,\n   `_io/export_ndjson.py` ~86-88. Fix: all 5 refer to the tuple by name instead of enumerating\n   members (follow `_engine_support/reads.py`'s existing correct pattern). Do not change\n   `export_ndjson` behaviour.\n\n3. reconciler dispatch-apply module: one comment cites a nonexistent allowlist symbol (sole\n   repo occurrence) -- restate accurately or delete. Another claims a helper is \"duplicated\"\n   from a sibling module but only 1 definition exists repo-wide -- delete false claim. Also\n   independently check 2 further unverified audit flags in the same package naming\n   `set_relationship`/`payload[\"links\"]` and re-export claims; fix if dangling, report if sound.\n\n4. `llm/review_kernel/decide.py`: a dead assignment falsely justified as keeping an exported,\n   independently-tested function \"exercised/live\" when the assignment target is never read.\n   Delete the statement + comment if still present. File is near the 800 LOC cap -- net change\n   must not increase it.\n\n5. `llm/workflow/interpreter.py`: `_commit_state`'s docstring falsely claims it's the sole\n   chokepoint for all writes (re-verified: multiple write sites bypass it). Re-census writes\n   against current source, correct the docstring to claim only what's verified -- no guessing at\n   an unverified mechanism.\n\n6. `llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`: a test slices this module's raw source between 2 named\n   function definitions -- making their existence/order load-bearing, invisible to rename tools.\n   Add a short comment at both ends (gate_dispatch.py and the test) naming the coupling. File is\n   near the 800 LOC cap -- net change must be neutral or negative.\n\n7. `_engine_support/next_batch.py`: (a) move a local binding + its comment above the helper that\n   reads it, verifying no dependency is bound later than the new spot. (b) a `__slots__` field is\n   never assigned anywhere, emitted under a different name -- a published schema field, do not\n   remove. Add a comment at the init explaining retained-for-compat, matching an existing sibling\n   note, mentioning the rename.\n\n8. `_commands/fsck_recover.py`: a helper is called early in the file but defined last (module\n   level, resolves fine at call time). Move the definition above its first caller.\n\n9. `llm/plan_review/floors.py`: has appliers of the same drop-a-finding algorithm as a sibling\n   function (called from 3 sites elsewhere, which explain why) but calls it from neither and\n   never explains why. Determine if the omission is correct; if so add a one-line note. If NOT\n   correct, that's a behavioural bug, OUT OF SCOPE for this change -- report separately, do not\n   fix.\n\n10. (Read-only, do not edit) \"Parser of record\": several modules carry this comment above an\n    argparse factory. Pin the exact file count + line numbers, used-vs-discarded per site, and\n    resolve the audit-vs-recount discrepancy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every site re-verified against current origin/main before editing; mismatches are\n  skipped and reported rather than forced.\n- [ ] Site 1 ships a new plain test (no new helper/fixture) asserting the 3-way constant\n  mirror between `finalize.py`, `plan_review_recovery.py`, and `runs.py`.\n- [ ] Sites 2-9 are comment/docstring-only plus the 2 described statement moves and the 1\n  dead-statement delete; no control-flow changes anywhere.\n- [ ] `decide.py` and `gate_dispatch.py` line counts are net-neutral or lower after the change.\n- [ ] No new config key, env var, feature flag, CI gate, lock, autouse fixture, or test helper\n  (the mechanism-delta ratchet stays clean).\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` passes with no new or increased\n  entries.\n- [ ] Item 10's census is reported in the commit/ticket trail with no edits to those files.\n- [ ] Item 3's 2 unverified cross-references are independently checked and the verdict\n  (dangling vs sound) is reported.\n- [ ] Item 9: if the `floors.py` omission turns out to be a real behavioural bug, it is reported\n  separately and left unfixed in this change.\n\n## Testing\n\n- [ ] `make verify` (lint + typecheck + import-convention + full test suite) run from inside the\n  fresh worktree with the worktree's own `.venv/bin` first on PATH, and its full output captured;\n  the change is pushed only once this passes.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py","reason":"correct stale mirror-location comment/docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py","reason":"note the third _LLM_STEP_KINDS copy"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_api.py","reason":"correct stale 2-type comment/docstring for _NON_GRAPH_ARTIFACT_TYPES"},{"path":"src/rebar/graph/_ready.py","reason":"correct inherited stale 2-type comment"},{"path":"src/rebar/graph/_unblock.py","reason":"correct inherited stale 2-type comment"},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/export_ndjson.py","reason":"correct inherited stale 2-type docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py","reason":"check 2 dangling cross-references, fix if still stale"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_pass.py","reason":"check unverified audit flag re set_relationship/payload[links]"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/applier.py","reason":"check unverified audit flag re re-export comments"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py","reason":"delete dead _sev assignment and false justification if still present"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/interpreter.py","reason":"correct _commit_state docstring to match verified write-site census"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"add load-bearing note for test source-slicing coupling"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_step_failures.py","reason":"add load-bearing note for source-slicing coupling"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py","reason":"move _blocked_ids binding above use, add files_read compat note"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_recover.py","reason":"move _read_or above its first caller"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/floors.py","reason":"add note on why verdict recompute is not needed here, or report real bug"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5dd05028-286f-4f67-b661-4f737f68c979","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2531-8683-0365-49d3","ticket_type":"task","title":"Fix 9 stale comment/docstring sites from read-based audit (finalize.py, _api.py, dispatch_apply_phases.py, decide.py, interpreter.py, gate_dispatch.py, next_batch.py, fsck_recover.py, floors.py)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d72dc386-261d-40ec-a0be-379c8e5e3b1b","6bcb06fd-cfb2-4067-b01c-1d8158db2d73","bb4510fb-c258-4e12-ad88-d29f86d2f873","b9da5483-961e-40f0-8879-e4018036bdc4","4b271f96-35c0-41ab-81f4-26deb19077b5","5dd05028-286f-4f67-b661-4f737f68c979","14773d02-82e5-45e3-9508-1aa53d585707"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793826703792445664,"uuid":"ca0b42d5-00b5-4099-b656-bb8ee8528966"}